cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Weather2Watts, please cite it as below."
title: "Weather2Watts: a small, open check of how AI weather forecasts translate into real wind power"
abstract: >-
  Forecasts from AI weather models (GraphCast, Pangu-Weather, FuXi, GenCast, ECMWF AIFS) and the
  physics-based ECMWF IFS/HRES are converted to wind power and scored against observed hourly
  generation in 15 European countries, with a daily live comparison of ECMWF AIFS and IFS.
authors:
  - family-names: Gaglione
    given-names: Davide
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DavideWasTaken/Weather2Watts"
keywords:
  - weather forecasting
  - wind power
  - renewable energy
  - AI weather prediction
  - benchmark
  - GraphCast
  - ECMWF AIFS
  - ENTSO-E
